\section{Introduction}
Valley Maidu (ISO 639-3 vmv; Glottolog vall1252) is an extinct Maiduan language of California. Searches found no Valley Maidu dictionary or revitalization programme. The nearest well-documented relative found is Konkow Maidu.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None were found specifically for Valley Maidu. The Konkow Maidu site below includes lessons and stories for a related variety. Whether they are usable for Valley Maidu was not verified.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Konkow Maidu dictionary and database (related variety): \url{https://www.konkow.org/pub/dict.php}
\item Article on the Konkow Maidu website and database: \url{https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/items/f283a176-4829-4621-89d2-a1495bb01961}
\item Valley Maidu numerals, recorded only for 1--10: \url{https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Maidu-Valley.htm}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Konkow Wailaki Maidu Indian Cultural Preservation Association, a related community: \url{https://actaonline.org/profile/konkow-wailaki-maidu-indian-cultural-preservation-association/}
\item Maidu community site: \url{https://maidu.org/about.html}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Endangered Languages Project guide: \url{https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/2290/guide/6952}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Little Valley Maidu material was found. A curriculum would probably rest on archival sources, such as the early recordings and notes held in archives, together with Maiduan community partners. Konkow Maidu materials could serve as a model. This is a limited basis.
